{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Whenever the cloud was taken up.</b> As the Targum renders: lifting up. And likewise ״וְנַעֲלָה הֶעָנָן״. And it would not be correct to write it according to ״עֲלוֹת הֶעָנָן״, ״וְעָלָה הֶעָנָן״ — for this is not an expression of removal but of growth and rising, as in ״הִנֵּה עָב קְטַנָּה כְּכַף אִישׁ עֹלָה מִיָּם״ (1 Kings 18)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:05.617994111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}